WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:12.880
Hey youtubers it’s charlie and by popular
demand here’s my Game of Thrones Season

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:15.120
4 preview for Brienne of Tarth.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:22.730
Today as of posting this video it’s also
George RR Martin’s birthday, so he can’t

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:24.940
refuse any of your requests.

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:27.210
Or is that his daughter’s wedding day.

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:28.850
I don’t think he has a daughter though.

00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:32.870
So let’s roll the dice on that one.

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:39.190
Spoiler warning for everything in the first
three seasons and partial spoilers for feast

00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:40.190
for crows.

00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:42.590
Like I said before Brienne is one of my favorite
characters on Game of Thrones.

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:44.170
It’s really the actors Gwendoline Christie
and Nikolai Coster Waldeau that I have to

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:45.170
thank for that.

00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:50.950
When I first read the books honestly I spent
more time focused on the Jaime character after

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:51.950
they started traveling together.

00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:59.180
But after seeing them re-interpret things
for the show I really feel like when they’re

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:02.690
together it’s really Brienne’s story and
Jaime is just passing through.

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:12.800
Think of like Star Wars being a story about
this R2 droid’s adventures across this sixty

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:15.930
or seventy year span (he will be in episode
7).

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:18.020
And all the jedi masters and cool bounty hunters
he meets along the way.

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:21.510
Brienne is like the last good thing in westeros,
her story is really all about this totally

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:30.820
pure dream of becoming this glorious knight
defending her king and the realm.

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:34.290
Like what the King’s Guard is supposed to
be all about but totally fails at.

00:01:34.290 --> 00:01:37.100
In reality there is almost no honor amongst
the gold cloaks.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:41.280
But throughout the series she just sticks
to her guns and takes Jaime back to Kings

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:42.280
Landing.

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:46.650
Obviously some of her sense of honor and duty
rubs off on Jaime and they have some epic

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:48.780
fandom moments like the world’s most intense
bath scene.

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:51.740
But I really think that Brienne will have
a much more independent story line in Season

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:52.740
4.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:02:00.350
At the end of season 3 the last we saw of
her was saying goodbye to Jaime in the finale

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:01.759
once they’d reached King’s Landing.

00:02:01.759 --> 00:02:06.700
Since the show accelerated their story line
so much I expect that trend to continue and

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:07.890
Brienne will take on another quest.

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:09.420
Because what is a knight without a quest.

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:14.260
But there’s one big thing Brienne still
needs to deal with now that she’s back in

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:15.260
King’s Landing.

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:18.600
Remember she fled Renly’s camp in season
2 after the smoke baby gave him the shaft.

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:26.210
Since she was one of the only people in the
tent when they found him she and Catelyn got

00:02:26.210 --> 00:02:27.670
blamed for murdering him.

00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:29.110
They basically never resolved that plot point.

00:02:29.110 --> 00:02:33.859
So everyone who doesn’t understand that
magic was involved still thinks she killed

00:02:33.859 --> 00:02:34.859
him.

00:02:34.859 --> 00:02:36.570
Including his boyfriend Loras.

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:39.850
Who just happens to be in King’s Landing
getting ready to marry cersei.

00:02:39.850 --> 00:02:54.139
The first couple of episodes will pretty much
wrap up that storyline and Jaime will be forced

00:02:54.139 --> 00:02:59.010
to rescue Brienne from Loras again.

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:02.520
Since it’s a relatively minor plot point
compared to the other things happening in

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:05.600
Kings Landing I don’t know how much of a
scene it will get.

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:08.440
But chronologically it happens before Brienne
does anything else in the books.

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:11.950
Here’s where we need to talk about a few
spoilers for Brienne in the second half of

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:12.950
Book 3.

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:15.010
So remember I mentioned she needs another
quest, otherwise she won’t have an opportunity

00:03:15.010 --> 00:03:16.010
to try and help Catelyn.

00:03:16.010 --> 00:03:21.799
The whole point in bringing Jaime back was
to trade for Sansa and Arya who everyone thinks

00:03:21.799 --> 00:03:24.870
are still in King’s Landing.

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:33.300
Here’s where the show kind of messes with
things.

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:40.080
In the books when Brienne gets to King’s
Landing Sansa has already fled with Littlefinger

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:44.890
to the Vale and the Eyrie.

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:46.560
But because she’s still there in the show
I think they’re going to change some of

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:47.560
Brienne’s story.

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:49.750
I still think they’re going to send her
on another quest and they’ll still give

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:50.750
her Oathkeeper.

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:53.310
But I think the way the show will explain
it is that Brienne will end up being ordered

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:54.800
to bring Sansa back to King’s Landing.

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:56.900
Here’s a quick breakdown of how I think
all this will go down.

00:03:56.900 --> 00:04:00.980
First, Brienne and Jaime deal with a really
pissed off Loras.

00:04:00.980 --> 00:04:06.731
Two, Brienne doesn’t get any scenes for
an episode or two, three a super duper spoiler

00:04:06.731 --> 00:04:13.220
mega event happens, four sansa flees kings
landing with Littlefinger and then five Brienne

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:21.650
is ordered to find her and bring her back
under the explanation that she’s been kidnapped.

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:24.660
Let me know what you think of my season 4
timeline for Brienne.

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:32.680
Like i’ve said earlier the show is changing
a lot so they’ve already messed with the

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:33.729
timeline from the books.

00:04:33.729 --> 00:04:37.500
So it definitely won’t happen exactly that
way during season 4 for those who have read

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:38.500
ahead.

